AB  - Single deep learning semantic segmentation model is difficult to extract sufficient semantic information from high-resolution remote sensing images, leading to the problems of obvious errors in classification of some pixels and low segmentation accuracy for some complex ground objects. Therefore, this paper proposes a high resolution remote sensing image ground object segmentation method based on ensemble learning. Three classical deep learning ground object segmentation models, UNet, SegNet and DeepLabv3+, were used to deeply mine the high-level semantic features of remote sensing images from different dimensions, and the prediction probability distributions of three models was fused by the combination of hard voting and soft voting at the model level. The obvious errors in the segmentation results of a single model are effectively corrected through the ensemble learning strategy, while improving the overall model's ability to understand the local details of the image, thus improving the accuracy of prediction and the generalization ability of the overall model. The experimental results on the public data set of remote sensing images show that compared with the three baseline models of UNet, SegNet and DeepLabv3+, the ensemble learning method proposed in this paper improves the MPA index by 5.21%, 6.38% and 2.83%, and the MIoU index by 4.59%, 5.47% and 2.79%, respectively. This study makes up for the defects of single model when facing complex ground object segmentation scenes, and provides a method reference for ground object segmentation of high-resolution remote sensing image.
