AB  - In the area of remote sensing, hyperspectral image classification is well known for its applications in agriculture, mining and medical imaging. The powerful architectures, i.e., the transformers, are replacing the traditional deep learning models. In our analysis we compare the three prominent transformer models - Swin Transformer, Vision Transformer (ViT) and the proposed methodology, spatial spectral transformer. The concept of self-attention is indulged in ViT, while the Swin Transformer follows the approach of shifted window attention. Our proposed model, SST, extends the approach by spatial-spectral attention mechanisms along with active learning to reduce the complexity of the model by reducing the usage of the labelled dataset. The experiments are performed on various hyperspectral data sets, and classification accuracy, computational efficiency, and feature representation quality are taken into consideration for evaluating the model's efficiency.
