AB  - Recently, convolutional neural networks (CNN) have been used for hyperspectral image classification. Many CNNs utilize the spectral features directly without mining the connections among spectral bands. Thus, this paper proposes a band-dependent self-attention network that explores the cross-correlation of nearby spectral band groups. To maintain the diversity of the spectral groups and find the correlations of these spectral groups, the proposed network uses different query, key and value transformation matrices for different spectral bands. In addition, a conventional self-attention model is employed to calculate the queries, keys, and values for each spectral group. The classification performance of the proposed network was evaluated on three hyperspectral image datasets, and the experimental results demonstrated that the proposed CNN-based network outperformed several state-of-the-art networks.
